    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18332" root="زهم" body-key="z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَهِمٌ</span></b>  [part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَهِمَ</span>]. You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَحْمٌ زَهِمٌ</span> <i>Stinking, fat, flesh-meat.</i> (JK.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَدُهُ زَهِمَةٌ</span> <i>His
hand is greasy:</i> (S, K:) or <i>has in it the odour
of fat.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>Very fat; having much
fat:</i> or <i>having some remains of fatness.</i> (K.)

